  "documentation": {
    "range": "<span class=\"copy\"><em>Rocio octofasciata</em> is <span class=\"copy\"> widely distributed across the Atlantic slope of Mexico and Central America. Native from Rio Chachalacas<span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"copy\">,Veracruz, Mexico,  to Rio Ulúa, Honduras (Miller et al. 2005). Established in Alachua, Brevard, Dade, and  Hillsborough counties, Florida (Page and Burr 1991). This species has <span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"copy\">also been introduced in Thailand and Australia.</span></span></span>",
    "population": "This species is widespread and usually abundant, with multiple subpopulations (Miller et al. 2005).",
    "habitats": "<span class=\"fieldLabel\"> <span class=\"copy\">This species occurs in springs, rivers, channels, lakes and seasonally-flooded wetlands; water clear or turbid; flow absent to moderate;bottom muddy to sandy, rocky, or with plants in decomposition (Miller et al. 2005).&#160;An omnivore, it feeds on invertebrates and algae (Valtierra-Vega and Schmitter-Soto 2000).</span>",
    "threats": "<em>Rocio octofasciata&#160;</em>is very popular among aquarists; however, most lineages in the market come from farms. It may be impacted at the local scale by invasive species such as tilapia and armoured catfish, and pollution from agricultural fields or cities (J.J. Schmitter-Soto pers. comm. 2018).",
    "measures": "No conservation actions are known or likely to be needed for <em>Rocio octofasciata</em>. It is however known to occur within&#160;Sian Ka'an Biosphere Reserve (Schmitter-Soto 1998), among many others (IUCN and UNEP-WCMC 2018).",
    "use_trade": "The species is very popular among aquarists (Miller et al. 2005).",
    "rationale": "This species is assessed as Least Concern given it is widespread with suspected stable populations. Although it may face local threats from high popularity in the aquarium trade, and local impact by invasive species and urban or agricultural pollution at some locations, there is no major threat to its global population and there is currently no indication of major population decline.",
    "trend_justification": null,
    "taxonomic_notes": null
  },
